## Fixed this session (all unit-tested; `npm test` = 225 pass / 0 fail)

1. **e2e s5 pattern** (`test/e2e.sh`): `wait_pattern` matched `"command":"sleep 40"` (with
   closing quote) — the real tool line is `"command":"sleep 40 && echo done-sleeping"`, so
   the pattern never matched → Ctrl+C never sent → tool ran to completion → no `aborted`.
   Fix: match without the closing quote. (The 300 s wait then burned as a silent GPU-idle
   window — explains "no load" if observed mid-s5.)
2. **REPL piped mode drops burst lines** (`src/cli/main.ts`): piped stdin emits all
   `line` events + `close` in one tick. Lines arriving with no pending consumer were
   silently dropped; the loop then broke on `rlClosed` before draining. s8 symptom:
   session had 1 turn instead of 2. Fix: `queuedLines` buffer in `settle`/`askLine` +
   loop guard `if (rlClosed && queuedLines.length === 0) break;`
3. **Compaction planner: small windows could never compact** (`src/context/compact.ts`):
   (a) `keepTokens` default 8192 is not window-aware — with a 4096 window the kept
   suffix was larger than the window; now capped at `window - maxTokens - slack`
   (floor 512) in `compactContext`. (b) The "last user message must survive" rule
   (WS9, tested) forced `keepFrom → 0` when the ONLY user message is at index 0
   (single-prompt tool loops) → plan rejected forever. Now: rule applies for
   `lastUser > 0`; at index 0 the task survives via the summary (the summarizer prompt
   already requires the user's goal + constraints). s12 now passes: "rc=0, ✂ rendered,
   compaction entry persisted, task completed across compaction".
4. **eval `--timeout` was one shared budget for the whole run** (`test/eval-run.ts`):
   under a contended server the first two tasks ate it and the third task vanished
   from the report (silent `break` on abort). Now per-task: total = timeout × tasks.
   e2e s13 watchdog raised 480 s → 900 s to match.

Unit tests: `test/compact.test.ts` updated (single-prompt fold test rewritten to new
